  "catalog": {
    "text": "Learning\nCourses\nSTRUCTURED TRADEHQ COURSES\nLearn to Trade — Properly\n\nExplore the published catalog's 6 course tracks and 26 lessons. Each course card lists its topics and syllabus. Quizzes, sources, completion badges, and a $100,000 virtual practice account for supported spot instruments. Options and futures contract mechanics are taught through conceptual examples and worksheet exercises.\n\nEducational simulation only — not financial, investment, legal or tax advice.\n\nBrowse the courses\nOr explore the full Learn hub\nQUICK ANSWER\nAre TradeHQ's free trading courses any good?\n\nTradeHQ offers 6 structured course tracks with 26 lessons, quizzes, cited sources and completion badges. AI-assisted additions receive an editorial review before publication. The free $100,000 virtual account supports spot instruments; derivatives exercises are conceptual.\n\nWhat you will actually be able to do\n\nExplain options-chain fields and calculate hypothetical defined-risk spread payoffs\n\nExplain futures margin, contango and backwardation using contract worksheets\n\nIdentify economic releases and describe limits of interpreting market reactions\n\nExamine cognitive biases through fictional decision records without diagnosing individuals\n\nCompare hypothetical sizing assumptions and optional review records\n\nCourse tracks\n26 lessons · Free forever\nINTERMEDIATE\n60–75 min\nOptions Trading Fundamentals\n\nA structured introduction to listed options — from call contracts and the Greeks to defined-risk spread examples. Work through contract payoffs on paper; TradeHQ's spot simulator does not execute options contracts.\n\nSYLLABUS\n\n›\nWhat Is an Option? Calls & Puts Explained\n›\nThe Greeks — Delta, Gamma, Theta & Vega\n›\nDefined-Risk Spreads — Verticals & Iron Condors\n+ 2 more lessons\n0% complete\nStart course\nINTERMEDIATE\n60–75 min\nFutures & Derivatives\n\nA ground-up guide to exchange-listed futures — how contracts are specified, how margin actually works, why term-structure matters, and how hedgers and speculators interact on the CME.\n\nSYLLABUS\n\n›\nWhat Is a Futures Contract?\n›\nMargin & Leverage in Futures\n›\nContango & Backwardation — Term Structure Explained\n+ 2 more lessons\n0% complete\nStart course\nINTERMEDIATE\n60–75 min\nMacro Reading for Traders\n\nAn introduction to CPI releases, central-bank decisions, Treasury yields and the dollar index, with exercises for separating observed data from uncertain market interpretations.\n\nSYLLABUS\n\n›\nReading CPI and Inflation Data\n›\nThe Fed & FOMC Cycle — How Rat",
    "headings": [
      "Options Trading Fundamentals",
      "Futures & Derivatives",
